What is a Hypochlorous Acid Water Generator?
A Hypochlorous Acid Water Generator is an electrolysis device that utilizes a diaphragm-type electrolytic cell to process tap water mixed with a precise proportion of sodium chloride. Through this process, it generates an acidic aqueous solution characterized by a low concentration of available chlorine and a high redox potential on the anode side.
This generated solution, known as electrolyzed water, is a powerful yet safe disinfectant. Because it is produced on-site and on-demand, it eliminates the logistical and safety concerns associated with storing and transporting traditional chemical sanitizers. Its efficacy against a broad spectrum of pathogens, including bacteria, viruses, and spores, makes it a versatile tool for modern sanitation needs.
